# Binary multiplication in lambda plus merge, with no label: scored points
# of the label-free family.
#
# THE PROGRAM compares the product of two Scott binary naturals with a
# claimed one: times (contest_merge_dynamic.pl, times_function/3) shifts
# and adds, a times b = 0 when a is 0, double(h b) when a is 2h and
# b + double(h b) when a is 2h + 1, with the curried plus and equality of
# the same module, each let bound once. No merge occurs: these points
# measure how fast a reading evaluates, not how it shares, the ground of
# the JIT settings, now without labels.
#
# THE REFERENCE is Prolog's own multiplication; the schoolbook algorithm
# the program follows costs O(n^2) in the number of bits n, a doubling of
# the digits costing 4.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-28, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh, a fresh process per
# reading, the intended template, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB), in a probe of the
# same program:
# - weak_head: products of 8, 16, 32 and 64 digits in 195, 632, 2465 and
#   11143 ms, 128 digits stopped;
# - tabling(weak_head): 147, 451, 1790 and 8374 ms, 128 digits stopped.
# A second run on the points themselves: weak_head 646 and 2554 ms at 16
# and 32 digits, tabling(weak_head) 520 and 1752 ms; both stopped at 64
# digits near 7.8 s, which is at the edge, and at 128.
# The labeled family (contest_inheritance_binary.pl) was stopped on the
# product of 16 digits under every reading at the family's limits.
# The sizes are 16, 32 and 64 digits (n, 2n and 4n; 64 at the edge) and
# 128 beyond, and a wrong claim at 32 digits, the product with bit 50
# flipped, which the comparison reaches after the 50 bits below it.
# BEYOND THE FRONTIER (four settings read the product of 128 digits): one
# step beyond, 256 digits, the two
# 128-digit factors concatenated in both orders. Readings (2026-09-28,
# point_claims/2): weak_head and tabling(weak_head) stopped, in 6653 and
# 6483 ms.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - recognising the catalogued times by its content address and multiplying
#   natively: J.-C. Filliâtre, S. Conchon, Type-Safe Modular Hash-Consing,
#   ML Workshop 2006, doi:10.1145/1159876.1159880.
# - or compiling the interpreter's hot loop, the ground of the JIT settings:
#   C. F. Bolz, A. Cuni, M. Fijalkowski, A. Rigo, Tracing the Meta-Level:
#   PyPy's Tracing JIT Compiler, ICOOOLPS 2009, doi:10.1145/1565824.1565827.

#   product_point(?Point, ?Left, ?Right, ?Flipped): the claim is
#   Left * Right with the bits of Flipped flipped, the true product when
#   Flipped is 0.
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
λ
